      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe function `MonetrixVault.supplyToBlp()`\n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Supply `l1Amount` of `token` into HL's BLP (action 15 op=0). L1 8-dp wei.\n    function supplyToBlp(uint64 token, uint64 l1Amount) external onlyOperator whenOperatorNotPaused {\n        require(l1Amount > 0, \"zero amount\");\n        ActionEncoder.sendSupply(token, l1Amount);\n        if (accountant != address(0)) {\n            uint32 perpIndex = 0;\n            if (token != uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n                // Whitelist map is authoritative — BTC-PERP is index 0.\n                require(config.isSpotWhitelisted(uint32(token)), \"spot not whitelisted\");\n                perpIndex = config.spotToPerp(uint32(token));\n            }\n            MonetrixAccountant(accountant).notifyVaultSupply(token, perpIndex);\n        }\n        emit BlpSupplied(token, l1Amount);\n    }\n```\n\n automatically registers a Vault-side 0x811 supplied slot in `MonetrixAccountant.vaultSupplied`.\n\n```solidity\nMonetrixAccountant(accountant).notifyVaultSupply(token, perpIndex);\n```\n\nbut `MonetrixVault.withdrawFromBlp()`\n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Withdraw from BLP back to spot (action 15 op=1). `l1Amount=0` means max.\n    function withdrawFromBlp(uint64 token, uint64 l1Amount) external onlyOperator whenOperatorNotPaused {\n        ActionEncoder.sendWithdrawSupply(token, l1Amount);\n        emit BlpWithdrawn(token, l1Amount);\n    }\n```\n never removes that registry entry when the BLP position is fully unwound. MonetrixAccountant.totalBackingSigned()\n\n```solidity\n function totalBackingSigned() public view returns (int256 total) {\n        // EVM USDC — Vault + RedeemEscrow (not YieldEscrow: undistributed yield is not backing)\n        total = int256(usdc.balanceOf(vault));\n        address re = IMonetrixVaultReader(vault).redeemEscrow();\n        if (re != address(0)) {\n            total += int256(usdc.balanceOf(re));\n        }\n\n        // L1 state — vault reads the Vault-side registry; multisigVault reads\n        // its own registry. Strict 0x811 on every entry: if an entry is listed\n        // but the slot was never actually activated on HL, backing reverts —\n        // forcing a keeper/operator registration fix rather than silently\n        // under-counting.\n        total += _readL1Backing(vault, vaultSupplied);\n        address _multisigVault = IMonetrixVaultReader(vault).multisigVault();\n        if (_multisigVault != address(0)) {\n            total += _readL1Backing(_multisigVault, multisigSupplied);\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n later iterates every registered supplied slot and performs a strict `PrecompileReader.suppliedBalance()` read\n\n```solidity\n// Supplied (0x811) — iterate only registered slots; strict reads.\n        uint256 slen = suppliedList.length;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < slen; i++) {\n            SuppliedAsset storage a = suppliedList[i];\n            if (a.spotToken == uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n                total += int256(PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account));\n            } else {\n                total += int256(\n                    PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(uint32(a.spotToken), a.perpIndex, account)\n                );\n            }\n        }\n```\n\n which **reverts** if the external 0x811 slot is absent or unreadable. As a result, after a normal BLP supply-then-full-withdraw lifecycle, the protocol can enter a state where `totalBackingSigned()`, `surplus()`, `distributableSurplus()`, and `settle()` all revert until a separate manual `removeSuppliedEntry()` cleanup is performed. Essentially a cosmic DoS leading to a lifecycle-coupling and accounting-liveness bug, not a theft bug.\n\n### There was a quick peform RPC call test and it returns \n\n```shell\nerror code -32003: EVM error: PrecompileError\n```\n\nSo the real RPC did not return a normal zero-filled payload for the absent 0x811 slot. It errored.\n\nThat is why, in the PoC, modeling the missing slot as an unreadable/reverting PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE call is consistent with what we observed on the live RPC.\n\n\n# Impact\n\n- Uses a normal supported BLP lifecycle: supply, then withdraw max/full unwind\n- Not a theft bug and not bad-parameter misuse\n- Root cause is incomplete lifecycle coupling between registry registration and registry retirement\n- Impact is protocol-wide accounting and settlement liveness failure\n\n\n# Note to the Judge and Sponsor\n\nThe issue resides in a Operator side vector and perfectly fits the 2 categories mentioned in the contest details:\n\n### Areas of concern (where to focus for bugs)\n\n1. Accountant 4-gate settle pipeline\n2. HyperCore precompile read semantics.\n\nThe issue its **NOT** about the operator theft or trusting the operator because of funds or other inputs, the issue **its a lifecycle bug** that directly breaks the Monetrix accounting state, in a obviously vector where the operator usually peforms actions. \n\nSo the bug lives in an Operator vector area, but the flaw is still a protocol lifecycle/invariant bug, not a trust-minimization complaint. That is consistent with the sponsor calling out the Accountant settle pipeline and HyperCore precompile semantics as areas of concern.\n\nTechnically. Monetrix models BLP-supplied assets as a registered external resource, but its lifecycle is asymmetric: the resource is auto-registered when created and not auto-unregistered when destroyed, so strict Accountant reads can keep treating a dead `0x811` slot as mandatory and brick global accounting.\n\nin short this is a lifecycle/accounting bug, not an operator theft/inactivity bug\n\n# PoC running result\n\n```shell\nroot@be8240e5a691:/home/2026-04-monetrix# forge test --match-path test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol -vvvvv\n[⠊] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 1 test for test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol:C4Submission\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 372963)\nTrace